    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-04T09:19:36+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T09:19:36+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T23:49:36Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T23:49:36Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure ridge over SA will move to the east this morning, as a trough moves over the state during the day, followed by a strong cold front early Saturday. A high pressure system will then move across the state, behind the front, and merge with another high located to the southwest of WA on Sunday to extend a ridge across much of SA into next week. A low pressure system is also expected to move in vicinity of the WA border late Sunday and may extend a trough into far west SA into next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. High chance of showers south of Yunta, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Yunta in the evening. Winds northerly 30 to 45 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 23 to 37.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 3:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 7 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers south of Leigh Creek in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds north to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h increasing to 45 km/h before shifting southerly 15 to 25 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 22 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-07T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-06T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. The chance of morning fog south of Leigh Creek. Winds southerly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-07T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-08T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-06T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-07T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 14 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
